    "teach_2": {
      "id": "teach_2",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Now look at 20 + 30 ÷ 5.\n\nDivision stands ahead of addition in the BODMAS queue.\n\n20 + 30 ÷ 5\n= 20 + 6\n= 26\n\nIf you added first you would get 50 ÷ 5 = 10 — the trap.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_2_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_2_step": {
      "id": "teach_2_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Division and multiplication are at the same level. When only they remain, work left to right, like reading a sentence.\n\n48 ÷ 6 × 2\n= 8 × 2\n= 16\n\nDoing 6 × 2 first gives 48 ÷ 12 = 4, which is wrong.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_2"
        }
      ]
    },
