    "teach_3": {
      "id": "teach_3",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Exam setters love chained division:\n\n1888 ÷ 32 ÷ 8\n\nWork strictly left to right.\n\n1888 ÷ 32 = 59\n59 ÷ 8 = 7.375\n\nSo the value is 7.375.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_3_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_3_step": {
      "id": "teach_3_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The trap is to divide 32 ÷ 8 = 4 first and then compute 1888 ÷ 4 = 472.\n\n472 is actually printed as an option in the real exam question.\n\nRemember: in a ÷ b ÷ c, finish a ÷ b before touching the second ÷.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_3"
        }
      ]
    },
