    "teach_8": {
      "id": "teach_8",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "One last shape — the question mark inside the expression:\n\n853 + ? ÷ 17 = 1000\n\nBODMAS still rules. The ÷ happens before the +, so '? ÷ 17' is one block.\n\nThe block + 853 = 1000\nSo the block = 1000 − 853 = 147",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_8_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_8_step": {
      "id": "teach_8_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Now unwrap the block:\n\n? ÷ 17 = 147\n? = 147 × 17 = 2499\n\nCheck forwards: 2499 ÷ 17 = 147, and 853 + 147 = 1000. \n\nYou just used BODMAS twice — once to see the blocks, once to undo them.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_8"
        }
      ]
    },
